  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">POTHOLES PLUS PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this proposal, the Manitoba Habitat Heritage Corporation (MHHC) will perpetually secure 1,290 acres of wetland and associated upland habitat. Complementing this, MHHC will enhance 60 acres of impacted wetlands through restoration activities and contribute to continental mallard populations through the maintenance of 5,336 artificial nesting structures (i.e. Hen Houses). The maintenance of these structures is one of two management activities to be undertaken. The second, compliance monitoring and enforcement, will ensure adherence to easement terms for the 110,409 acres of previously secured waterfowl habitat. The net result of this wetland and upland habitat work is the maintenance and enhancement of crucial breeding habitat in North America, leading to the realization of waterfowl habitat and population goals of the NAWMP.</narrative>
  </description>
